        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Cross-platform testing strategy</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Start creative testing on one platform (usually Meta, due to its mature optimization algorithm), validate winners, then adapt them for other platforms. Don't run the same creative on TikTok and Meta without adaptation &mdash; TikTok demands more native, raw content, while Meta performs well with slightly more produced formats.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">A winning hook on Meta will often work on TikTok, but the production style needs to change. The insight (which angle, which hook) transfers; the execution must be platform-native.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 11 Glossary -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="glossary">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">11 &mdash; Glossary</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">Key terms</h2>

        {[
          { term: "Creative testing", def: "Systematic, hypothesis-driven experimentation on paid ad creatives. Each variation isolates one variable and is measured by purchase data." },
          { term: "CPA", def: "Cost per acquisition — the dollar amount spent on ads to acquire one customer through a specific creative." },
          { term: "ROAS", def: "Return on ad spend — revenue generated per dollar spent on ads. 3x+ is the benchmark for most categories." },
          { term: "Hook rate", def: "The percentage of viewers who watch past the first 3 seconds of an ad. The strongest early predictor of CPA performance." },
          { term: "Testing hierarchy", def: "The order in which variables should be tested: hooks first, then messaging angles, then visual style/format, then CTAs." },
          { term: "60/30/10", def: "Budget allocation rule: 60% on variations of proven winners, 30% on new concepts, 10% on experimental ideas." },
          { term: "Scale / Iterate / Kill", def: "The three outcomes for every tested creative. Scale = increase budget. Iterate = change one variable, retest. Kill = stop spending." },
          { term: "Kill threshold", def: "CPA 50% above target within 72 hours — stop spend immediately." },
          { term: "Scale threshold", def: "CPA 20% below target with sufficient volume — increase budget and produce variations." },
          { term: "Creative fatigue", def: "The gradual decline in ad performance as the audience sees it too many times. Typical lifespan: 2-6 weeks." },
          { term: "Statistical significance", def: "Minimum data required for reliable decisions: 1,000+ impressions, 100+ clicks, 50+ conversions per creative." },
          { term: "Modular script", def: "A script designed for testing: one body with multiple interchangeable hooks and CTAs." },
        ].map((item) => (
          <div class="py-4 border-b border-border">
            <div class="font-display font-semibold text-ink mb-1">{item.term}</div>
            <div class="text-[14px] text-muted">{item.def}</div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

